sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: main orchestrator 2026-11-13 (load a dump as the owner, no password shown). Secret shape of database.create (Q-DBAUTH, R3); client in a throwaway container on the server's network.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: database:import
  %% kind: database.import
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Server Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: database:import shop<br/>--file=/home/USER/shop.sql.gz
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit database:import shop --file=/home/USER/shop.sql.gz`
  %%> - syntax: `<slug> --file=PATH [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the slug of a MySQL or PostgreSQL connection on a Database server
  %%> - the absolute path of a `.sql` or `.sql.gz` file on the server's Node
  Note over GW: Validate, record import<br/>task #5181 · lock on shop
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the connection is on an active MySQL or PostgreSQL Database server (`database.import_unsupported`)
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node, which reaches NODE (`node_access.required`)
  %%> - the path is absolute, ends in `.sql` or `.sql.gz`, has no `.` or `..` part (`database.import_path_invalid`)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5181 with the path; the owner password stays encrypted in the connection
  GW->>SW: Store the owner password<br/>database-import-intent-5181
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - puts the owner password line into the Swamp vault after the task is committed (R3)
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the password never sits in argv, a file on the Node, the task input or result, or a log
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-database-import
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the client argv the Gateway built, the server's address and SSH host keys
  %%> - the vault key name, never the value
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5181
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Load the dump<br/>as the Node's SSH user
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - the Node's SSH user, without sudo; the dump is read only when that user owns it
  %%> The file:
  %%> - opened once; its real path must equal the given path (no symlink), a regular file
  %%> - otherwise `database.import_file_refused`, and nothing is loaded
  %%> The client:
  %%> - a throwaway container of the server's image on the server's Docker network, read-only, no capabilities
  %%> - it logs in as the owner over TCP at the server container's address, never its trusted loopback
  %%> - the password is the first stdin line
  %%> What it does, in order:
  %%> - counts the tables; more than 0 refuses with `database.not_empty`
  %%> - streams the file (gunzip for `.sql.gz`) into the client; the first error stops it
  %%> - counts the tables again
  %%> Limits:
  %%> - 3600 s for the step
  alt the dump loads
    N-->>SW: bytes read, tables
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - bytes read from the file, the client's exit code, the table count; no names, no data
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5181 succeeds with `bytes_read`, `exit_code` and `tables`
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: refused or SQL error
    %%> When:
    %%> - the file or the database is refused, the owner cannot log in, or a statement fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, database_state
    %%> Result:
    %%> - `database_state` is `unchanged`, `empty`, `partial`, or `unknown` when the run ends without its result
    %%> - PostgreSQL loads in one transaction, so a failed load leaves it empty
    %%> - MySQL commits each table, so a failed load can leave it partly filled
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - from `partial`: empty the database first, then import again
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5181
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
